  "kind": "definition",
  "title": "Normalization in the function field",
  "statement": "Let $X$ be an integral scheme with function field\n$K=k(X)$ ([def-sc-function-field]). The *normalization\nof $X$ in $K$* is\n\n$$\nX^{\\nu}:=\\operatorname{\\underline{Spec}}_X\\bigl(\\widetilde{\\mathcal O_X}\\bigr),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\widetilde{\\mathcal O_X}$ is the integral closure of\n$\\mathcal O_X$ in the constant sheaf $K$, together with the\ncanonical morphism $\\nu:X^{\\nu}\\to X$. Finiteness is a\nseparate property of this morphism; it is not part of the definition.",
